  "content": {
    "id": "p10-q15-answer",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "A plane has run out of fuel and is gliding at an angle of depression of $10^{\\circ}20'$. If it is at a height of 800 m and the airport is 4.7 km away horizontally, will it be able to reach the airport? Give the horizontal glide distance to 1 decimal place.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "No. Its horizontal glide distance is $4387.6\\text{ m}$, less than $4700\\text{ m}$.",
      "worked": "Let $x$ be the horizontal glide distance in metres. The angle of elevation from the landing point equals the angle of depression.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan\\left(10^{\\circ}20'\\right)&=\\frac{800}{x}\\\\x&=\\frac{800}{\\tan\\left(10^{\\circ}20'\\right)}\\\\x&\\approx4387.6\\text{ m}\\end{align*}$$\nThe airport is $4.7\\text{ km}=4700\\text{ m}$ away horizontally. Since $4387.6<4700$, the plane will land before reaching the airport.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 36
  },
